<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101649" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφεός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εή</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εά, -εόν,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφός, σφέτερος</span>
			, <i>their (own</i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφεὰ δώματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.849
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴομεν αὖτις ἕκαστοι ἐπὶ
			σφεά</span> each to <i>his own</i>, ib. <i><span class="en">
				872
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφωΐτερος</span>
			, <i>your</i> (in addressing a pair), <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>his, her</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφεᾶς ἔειξε χώρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					31
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφ&lt;ε&gt;ὸς ἔσκε
			πατήρ</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				7289
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
